---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout>
  <!-- Top bar -->
  <nav id="nav">
    <div class="nav-inner">
      <a href="#" class="nav-name">Smit Kiri</a>
      <div class="nav-right">
        <a href="https://github.com/smitkiri" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="nav-ext">GitHub ↗</a>
        <a href="https://linkedin.com/in/smitkiri" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="nav-ext">LinkedIn ↗</a>
        <a href="mailto:smit.kiri@gmail.com" class="nav-ext">Email ↗</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </nav>

  <!-- Side nav -->
  <aside class="side-nav">
    <a href="#work-on" class="side-nav-link">Work on</a>
    <a href="#selected-work" class="side-nav-link">Selected work</a>
    <a href="#writing" class="side-nav-link">Writing</a>
    <a href="#patents" class="side-nav-link">Patents</a>
  </aside>

  <main>
    <!-- Hero -->
    <section class="hero">
      <div class="hero-intro">
        <div class="hero-text">
          <h1 class="hero-name">Smit Kiri</h1>
          <p class="hero-role">
            Lead ML Infra Engineer
            <span class="role-sep">at</span>
            <a href="https://klaviyo.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="role-company">Klaviyo</a>
          </p>
        </div>
        <img src="/profile.jpg" alt="Smit Kiri" class="hero-photo" />
      </div>
      <p class="hero-bio">
        I build and lead the ML infrastructure that powers Klaviyo's machine
        learning — Ray clusters running distributed compute across hundreds of
        nodes, serving platforms that compress deployment timelines from months to
        days, and the technical roadmaps that define how the platform evolves. My
        focus is on foundations that compound: infrastructure and strategy that
        multiply what ~40 ML engineers and data scientists can accomplish.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- What I work on -->
    <section class="section" id="work-on">
      <p class="section-eyebrow">What I work on</p>

      <div class="focus-list">
        <div class="focus-item">
          <h2 class="focus-title">Distributed Compute</h2>
          <p class="focus-body">
            Klaviyo's ML teams needed to run large-scale training and batch inference
            workloads across hundreds of nodes, reliably. I built DART Jobs, the compute
            platform that made this possible — powered by Ray Clusters on Kubernetes. It
            now handles 350–450 ML jobs per day on average, enabling research and
            production workloads that had no path to execution before this infrastructure
            existed. In 2025, a ground-up redesign of the platform drove a 7x increase
            in modeling runs and doubled the number of new users.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="focus-item">
          <h2 class="focus-title">Model Serving</h2>
          <p class="focus-body">
            Deploying a new production online inference system used to require months of
            custom infrastructure work from individual teams. I built DART Online
            (DAtascience RunTime Online), a shared serving platform on Ray Serve that
            compressed that timeline to a few days. Teams get a reliable, scalable,
            observable path from trained model to production without rebuilding the
            foundation each time.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="focus-item">
          <h2 class="focus-title">ML Platform & Tooling</h2>
          <p class="focus-body">
            The internal layer that multiplies what ML engineers and data scientists can
            do: experiment tracking with MLflow on Kubernetes, a model registry, VectorDB
            infrastructure, and model monitoring. I've also built CI/CD pipelines for ML
            workflows and contributed to a GitOps setup that condenses Kubernetes
            deployments to a single YAML — less friction between an idea and a
            production system.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="focus-item">
          <h2 class="focus-title">Platform Strategy</h2>
          <p class="focus-body">
            Defining long-horizon technical direction for Klaviyo's ML platform —
            authoring roadmaps for distributed compute, model serving, and the
            broader 2026 ML Platform Vision. I also work across engineering teams
            to review system designs and ensure the ML platform coheres with
            infrastructure direction at the company level.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="focus-item">
          <h2 class="focus-title">
            ML Orchestration
            <span class="focus-wip">in progress</span>
          </h2>
          <p class="focus-body">
            Currently building end-to-end ML pipeline orchestration with Prefect —
            bringing structured scheduling, dependency management, and observability
            to the full ML lifecycle, from data ingestion through model deployment.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Selected Work -->
    <section class="section" id="selected-work">
      <p class="section-eyebrow">Selected work</p>

      <div class="work-list">
        <article class="work-item">
          <div class="work-header">
            <h2 class="work-title">Reinventing Klaviyo's compute platform</h2>
            <span class="work-year">2025</span>
          </div>
          <p class="work-body">
            DART Jobs had been running successfully for two years, but its
            underlying architecture had limits that constrained how ML teams could
            use it. I led the ground-up redesign: defining the system architecture,
            evaluating tradeoffs, and serving as technical lead through execution.
            DART Jobs V2 drove a 7x increase in modeling runs and doubled the
            number of new users on the platform, unlocking a new generation of
            ML-powered products that weren't feasible before.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="work-item">
          <div class="work-header">
            <h2 class="work-title">DART becomes Klaviyo's ML foundation</h2>
            <span class="work-year">2024</span>
          </div>
          <p class="work-body">
            By 2024, DART had grown from infrastructure into institution — 40
            systems across 6 teams running on the platform. Teams that had spent
            months building custom deployment pipelines were instead shipping
            models in days. One team achieved a 10x speed-up in model training,
            another migrated ~10 models and shut down their legacy deployment
            system entirely, and a third deployed a suite of new compliance
            models that had no path to production before DART existed.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="work-item">
          <div class="work-header">
            <h2 class="work-title">Distributed ML compute at Klaviyo</h2>
            <span class="work-year">2023</span>
          </div>
          <p class="work-body">
            Distributed training and large-scale batch inference across hundreds of nodes
            wasn't possible with Klaviyo's existing infrastructure. I built DART Jobs,
            the platform that changed that — covering cluster provisioning, job
            scheduling, fault tolerance, and observability, all running on Ray and
            Kubernetes. DART Jobs now handles 350–450 ML jobs per day and has become the
            foundation for Klaviyo's most compute-intensive research and production
            workloads.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="work-item">
          <div class="work-header">
            <h2 class="work-title">From three months to three days</h2>
            <span class="work-year">2023</span>
          </div>
          <p class="work-body">
            At Klaviyo, each ML team was building its own serving infrastructure from
            scratch. The process was slow, duplicated across teams, and pulled engineers
            away from model development. I designed and built DART Online, a shared
            inference platform on Ray Serve that standardized the path from trained model
            to production. Standing up a new serving endpoint went from a months-long
            engineering effort to a matter of days.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Writing & Talks -->
    <section class="section" id="writing">
      <p class="section-eyebrow">Writing & talks</p>

      <div class="writing-list">
        <a
          href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9vcMfdQC_p4"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="writing-featured"
        >
          <div class="featured-badge">
            <span>Talk</span>
            <span class="meta-sep">·</span>
            <span>Ray Summit 2024</span>
            <span class="meta-sep">·</span>
            <span>Sep 2024</span>
          </div>
          <p class="featured-title">How Klaviyo built a robust model serving platform with Ray Serve</p>
          <p class="featured-desc">
            A deep dive into DART Online — how we designed and scaled Klaviyo's
            shared model serving platform using Ray Serve, the trade-offs we navigated,
            and lessons learned running it in production.
          </p>
          <span class="featured-cta">Watch on YouTube ↗</span>
        </a>

        <a
          href="https://medium.com/klaviyo-engineering/how-klaviyo-built-a-robust-model-serving-platform-with-ray-serve-c02ec65788b3"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="writing-row"
        >
          <div class="writing-meta">
            <span class="writing-type">Article</span>
            <span class="meta-sep">·</span>
            <span class="writing-venue">Klaviyo Engineering</span>
            <span class="meta-sep">·</span>
            <span class="writing-date">Sep 2024</span>
          </div>
          <div class="writing-bottom">
            <span class="writing-title">How Klaviyo built a robust model serving platform with Ray Serve</span>
            <span class="writing-arrow">↗</span>
          </div>
        </a>

        <a
          href="https://medium.com/klaviyo-data-science/klaviyo-data-science-podcast-ep-46-ml-ops-101-35c26a1079df"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="writing-row"
        >
          <div class="writing-meta">
            <span class="writing-type">Podcast</span>
            <span class="meta-sep">·</span>
            <span class="writing-venue">Klaviyo Data Science</span>
            <span class="meta-sep">·</span>
            <span class="writing-date">Apr 2024</span>
          </div>
          <div class="writing-bottom">
            <span class="writing-title">Ep. 46 — ML Ops 101</span>
            <span class="writing-arrow">↗</span>
          </div>
        </a>

        <a
          href="https://medium.com/klaviyo-data-science/klaviyo-data-science-podcast-ep-31-2022-a-data-science-year-in-review-93a33ff922f8"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="writing-row"
        >
          <div class="writing-meta">
            <span class="writing-type">Podcast</span>
            <span class="meta-sep">·</span>
            <span class="writing-venue">Klaviyo Data Science</span>
            <span class="meta-sep">·</span>
            <span class="writing-date">Jan 2023</span>
          </div>
          <div class="writing-bottom">
            <span class="writing-title">Ep. 31 — 2022: A Data Science Year in Review</span>
            <span class="writing-arrow">↗</span>
          </div>
        </a>

        <a
          href="https://medium.com/klaviyo-engineering/mlflow-setup-on-kubernetes-with-rds-and-s3-6a589bb40f3c"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="writing-row"
        >
          <div class="writing-meta">
            <span class="writing-type">Article</span>
            <span class="meta-sep">·</span>
            <span class="writing-venue">Klaviyo Engineering</span>
            <span class="meta-sep">·</span>
            <span class="writing-date">Dec 2022</span>
          </div>
          <div class="writing-bottom">
            <span class="writing-title">MLflow setup on Kubernetes with RDS and S3</span>
            <span class="writing-arrow">↗</span>
          </div>
        </a>

        <a
          href="https://medium.com/klaviyo-data-science/klaviyo-data-science-podcast-ep-27-nlp-conversations-at-scale-5b3cdd746f2e"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="writing-row"
        >
          <div class="writing-meta">
            <span class="writing-type">Podcast</span>
            <span class="meta-sep">·</span>
            <span class="writing-venue">Klaviyo Data Science</span>
            <span class="meta-sep">·</span>
            <span class="writing-date">Sep 2022</span>
          </div>
          <div class="writing-bottom">
            <span class="writing-title">Ep. 27 — NLP: Conversations at Scale</span>
            <span class="writing-arrow">↗</span>
          </div>
        </a>

        <a
          href="https://medium.com/klaviyo-engineering/interpretability-and-fairness-in-nlp-learnings-from-naacl-1daff75acd5e"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="writing-row"
        >
          <div class="writing-meta">
            <span class="writing-type">Article</span>
            <span class="meta-sep">·</span>
            <span class="writing-venue">Klaviyo Engineering</span>
            <span class="meta-sep">·</span>
            <span class="writing-date">Aug 2022</span>
          </div>
          <div class="writing-bottom">
            <span class="writing-title">Interpretability and Fairness in NLP: Learnings from NAACL</span>
            <span class="writing-arrow">↗</span>
          </div>
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Patents -->
    <section class="section" id="patents">
      <p class="section-eyebrow">Patents</p>

      <div class="patent-list">
        <a
          href="https://patents.google.com/patent/US12430500B2"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="writing-row"
        >
          <div class="writing-meta">
            <span class="writing-type">US Patent 12,430,500</span>
            <span class="meta-sep">·</span>
            <span class="writing-date">2025</span>
          </div>
          <div class="writing-bottom">
            <span class="writing-title">Implicitly annotating textual data in conversational messaging</span>
            <span class="writing-arrow">↗</span>
          </div>
        </a>

        <a
          href="https://patents.google.com/patent/US11989502B2"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="writing-row"
        >
          <div class="writing-meta">
            <span class="writing-type">US Patent 11,989,502</span>
            <span class="meta-sep">·</span>
            <span class="writing-date">2024</span>
          </div>
          <div class="writing-bottom">
            <span class="writing-title">Implicitly annotating textual data in conversational messaging</span>
            <span class="writing-arrow">↗</span>
          </div>
        </a>

        <a
          href="https://patents.google.com/patent/US20250029409A1"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="writing-row"
        >
          <div class="writing-meta">
            <span class="writing-type">US Patent App. 18/223,250</span>
            <span class="meta-sep">·</span>
            <span class="writing-date">2023</span>
          </div>
          <div class="writing-bottom">
            <span class="writing-title">Implicitly associating user intents to agent selected responses</span>
            <span class="writing-arrow">↗</span>
          </div>
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer>
    <div class="footer-inner">
      <a href="mailto:smit.kiri@gmail.com" class="footer-link">smit.kiri@gmail.com</a>
      <span class="footer-sep">·</span>
      <a href="https://github.com/smitkiri" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="footer-link">GitHub</a>
      <span class="footer-sep">·</span>
      <a href="https://linkedin.com/in/smitkiri" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="footer-link">LinkedIn</a>
    </div>
  </footer>
</Layout>

<style>
  /* ── Nav ── */
  #nav {
    position: fixed;
    top: 0; left: 0; right: 0;
    z-index: 100;
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.9);
    backdrop-filter: blur(12px);
    -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(12px);
    border-bottom: 1px solid transparent;
    transition: border-color 0.3s;
  }

  #nav.scrolled { border-color: var(--border); }

  .nav-inner {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 2rem;
    height: 56px;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
  }

  .nav-name {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--text);
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    transition: opacity 0.2s;
  }
  .nav-name:hover { opacity: 0.5; }

  .nav-right { display: flex; gap: 1.5rem; align-items: center; }

  .nav-ext {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--light);
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }
  .nav-ext:hover { color: var(--text); }

  /* ── Side nav ── */
  .side-nav {
    position: fixed;
    left: 2rem;
    top: 50%;
    transform: translateY(-50%);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    z-index: 100;
  }

  .side-nav-link {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    color: var(--light);
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
    transition: color 0.2s;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .side-nav-link:hover { color: var(--text); }

  @media (max-width: 1100px) {
    .side-nav { display: none; }
  }

  /* ── Main container ── */
  main {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 2rem;
  }

  /* ── Hero ── */
  .hero {
    padding: 132px 0 96px;
  }

  .hero-intro {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .hero-photo {
    width: 92px;
    height: 92px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    object-fit: cover;
    object-position: top center;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .hero-name {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 2.75rem);
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    color: var(--text);
    line-height: 1;
    margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
  }

  .hero-role {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.01em;
  }

  .role-sep { margin: 0 0.3em; color: var(--light); }

  .role-company {
    color: var(--accent);
    transition: opacity 0.2s;
  }
  .role-company:hover { opacity: 0.7; }

  .hero-bio {
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    line-height: 1.85;
    color: var(--body);
    max-width: 620px;
  }

  /* ── Sections ── */
  .section {
    padding: 72px 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    scroll-margin-top: 64px; /* clear the 56px fixed nav + 8px breathing room */
  }

  .section-eyebrow {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 1.75rem;
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 2.75rem;
    line-height: 1.1;
  }

  /* ── Focus areas ── */
  .focus-list {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 2.5rem;
  }

  .focus-title {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.625rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }

  .focus-wip {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.62rem;
    font-weight: 400;
    color: var(--accent);
    border: 1px solid var(--accent);
    border-radius: 3px;
    padding: 1px 5px;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    opacity: 0.75;
  }

  .focus-body {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    line-height: 1.85;
    color: var(--body);
  }

  /* ── Selected work ── */
  .work-list {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 3rem;
  }

  .work-header {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.875rem;
  }

  .work-title {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    font-weight: 400;
    color: var(--text);
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    line-height: 1.2;
  }

  .work-year {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    color: var(--light);
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .work-body {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    line-height: 1.85;
    color: var(--body);
  }

  /* ── Writing & Talks ── */
  .writing-list { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0; }

  /* Featured talk card */
  .writing-featured {
    display: block;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.75rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--accent);
    border-radius: 6px;
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 5%, transparent);
    transition: background 0.2s, transform 0.2s;
  }
  .writing-featured:hover {
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 9%, transparent);
    transform: translateY(-1px);
  }

  .featured-badge {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.4rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.65rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    color: var(--accent);
    margin-bottom: 0.625rem;
  }

  .featured-title {
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--text);
    line-height: 1.4;
    margin-bottom: 0.625rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }

  .featured-desc {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: var(--body);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .featured-cta {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--accent);
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
  }

  /* Article rows */
  .writing-row {
    display: block;
    padding: 1.25rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    transition: padding-left 0.25s ease;
  }
  .writing-row:first-of-type { border-top: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .writing-row:hover { padding-left: 0.625rem; }

  .writing-meta {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.4rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.3rem;
  }

  .writing-type {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.65rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    color: var(--light);
  }

  .meta-sep { font-size: 0.65rem; color: var(--border); }

  .writing-venue {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.65rem;
    color: var(--accent);
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
  }

  .writing-date {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.65rem;
    color: var(--light);
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
  }

  .writing-bottom {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .writing-title {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--text);
    line-height: 1.4;
  }

  .writing-arrow {
    color: var(--light);
    font-size: 1rem;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    transition: transform 0.2s, color 0.2s;
  }
  .writing-row:hover .writing-arrow {
    transform: translate(2px, -2px);
    color: var(--text);
  }

  /* ── Patents ── */
  .patent-list { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0; }

  /* ── Footer ── */
  footer {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding: 2.25rem 0 3.5rem;
  }

  .footer-inner {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 2rem;
    display: flex;
